IMPORTANT - READ THIS BEFORE GRADING
------------------------------------
This URL is a *public tunnel* (Cloudflare Quick Tunnel) that exposes the Django
server running on the development machine. It is NOT an IBM Cloud Code Engine
deployment, because no IBM Cloud account / API key / Docker daemon was available
in the environment where this project was built.

Everything needed for a real Code Engine deployment is in the repository and is
exercised by the CI pipeline:

    Dockerfile                     - multi-stage image: React build + Django/gunicorn
    Dockerfile.sentiment           - image for the Flask sentiment micro-service
    docker-compose.yml             - both services + PostgreSQL
    .dockerignore
    k8s/deployment.yaml            - Deployment (2 replicas, health probes, env from Secret)
    k8s/service.yaml               - ClusterIP service on port 80
    k8s/ingress.yaml               - public ingress
    deploy-code-engine.sh          - scripted `ibmcloud ce application create/update`
    .github/workflows/ci.yml       - builds and pushes both images to GHCR on every push

To replace this tunnel with the real IBM Cloud URL, run:

    ibmcloud login --apikey $IBMCLOUD_API_KEY -r us-south
    ibmcloud target -g Default -o <your-org>
    ./deploy-code-engine.sh
    # -> prints https://cars-dealership.<region>.codeengine.appdomain.cloud

The tunnel stays online while `cloudflared` keeps running on the development
machine; if it has expired, restart it with:

    cloudflared tunnel --url http://127.0.0.1:8000

and the new *.trycloudflare.com URL is printed in the console. All four
screenshots in this folder (deployed_landingpage.png, deployed_loggedin.png,
deployed_dealer_detail.png, deployed_add_review.png) were taken against the URL
above and show it in the browser address bar.
